import Vsa.Sim.ExecEntry

/-!
# `LayoutStmtTableGen` — the M6 `exec_stmt` dispatch jump-table slot pins

GENERATED by `scripts/gen_layout.py` from `objdump -s --section=.rodata
c/while-riscv-htif.elf`.  DO NOT hand-edit — regenerate.

The `ST_*` dispatch reads a 4-byte offset from the `.rodata` jump table at
`stmtJumpTableBase = 0x80019fb8` (`ExecEntry.lean:142`), slot `k` (the
`StmtKind` tag, `c/src/ast.h`) living at `stmtJumpTableBase + 4*k`, then jumps
to `stmtJumpTableBase + (Int32) offset`.  This file emits ONE
`Vsa.Sim.StmtSlotPinned k armPC m` theorem per tag — grounding the slot pin
every exec-arm residual (`ExecCaseGeom`/`Exec*Geom` `hslot`) demands — so a
single generator run supplies all 9 arms' slot facts (each arm consumes its
`groundStmtSlot_<k>` from its own 4 byte pins).  Mirrors `LayoutJumpTableGen`
(the eval_expr table); entry audit need N2
(`experiments/entry-needs-audit.md`).

Slot table (tag, name, slot addr, LE bytes, arm PC), read from the fixed ELF:

   0  ST_EXPR      0x80019fb8  b8 a1 fe ff  0x80004170
   1  ST_VAR       0x80019fbc  20 a1 fe ff  0x800040d8
   2  ST_BLOCK     0x80019fc0  d4 a1 fe ff  0x8000418c
   3  ST_IF        0x80019fc4  30 a2 fe ff  0x800041e8
   4  ST_WHILE     0x80019fc8  84 a0 fe ff  0x8000403c
   5  ST_FOR       0x80019fcc  7c a2 fe ff  0x80004234
   6  ST_RETURN    0x80019fd0  68 a1 fe ff  0x80004120
   7  ST_BREAK     0x80019fd4  e0 a0 fe ff  0x80004098
   8  ST_CONTINUE  0x80019fd8  00 a1 fe ff  0x800040b8

ALL NINE arm PCs are cross-checked against the `execArm*` constants pinned in
`ExecEntry.lean` (`ST_EXPECTED_ARM_PC`); a drift hard-aborts the generator.

NO `sorry`/`axiom`/`native_decide`/`bv_decide`; no Mathlib.
-/

open LeanRV64DExecutable LeanRV64DExecutable.Functions Sail ConcurrencyInterfaceV1 Vsa
open Register
